  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 1004 AM MST Tue Nov 17 2026\n\nThis afternoon and tonight... This afternoon will be dry and \nbreezy, because of a storm system moving through the Rockies. \nHighs across the area will climb to the mid to upper 60s, \napproaching that 70 degree mark. This evening and into the \novernight an upper level low will cause southwesterly winds and \nbring a surge of some moisture into the mid levels. This will \nbring a slight chance for isolated showers in the Gila and Black \nrange regions this evening into late tonight. Areas of higher \nelevations with West to East facing passes could see a high gust \nor two up to 40 mph as the low passes north of the region.\n\nWednesday through Friday...\nTomorrow upper level ridging will bring high pressure back to the\nregion bringing fair weather with light winds until Friday. Highs\nwill climb into the low to mid 70s through Friday. Another upper \nlevel trough will begin to move into the area on Friday. \nSouthwesterly winds will return and bring breezy winds to the area\nwith gusts to 30 mph. Although the threat of rain will remain \nmainly north of our region, a non-zero chance of an isolated light\nshower will be possible in the Gila/Back Range region, given some\ncyclonic vorticity and modest moister in the mid levels. \n\nSaturday into Early Next Week... Moving into the weekend another \nridge will create calm and fair weather for most of the weekend, \ntemperatures will be slightly cooler, following the storm system \nfrom friday. Early next week another trough will move into the \narea bringing our next chance of precipitation, but it is still \ntoo early to determine how much rain there will be or how \nwidespread it will be.",
